course: dictionary
lesson: 3574
title: Feudal and the feudal system
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Feudal is an adjective. It describes the feudal system, the way society was organised in medieval Europe. Kings gave land to lords, and lords gave loyalty and soldiers in return. Peasants worked the land for their lords.
explain: In history lessons this system is often drawn as a pyramid: king at the top, then lords, then knights, then peasants at the bottom. Feudal means belonging to that old pyramid of land and loyalty.
explain: Look at the context: «after the plague there were so few workers that the survivors could ask for higher pay, and the old feudal system began to crack.» Old tells you the system belonged to the past, and crack tells you it was weakening and breaking. So feudal means belonging to that system of lords and peasants.
explain: People also use feudal informally to mean old-fashioned and unfair, where a few powerful people control many others. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: the old system of lords began to crack. It still makes sense.
fact: Feudal comes from the feudal system, the way society was organised in medieval Europe.
fact: «Feudal» means belonging to that system, where land was given in return for loyalty and soldiers.
fact: «Feudal lord» means a lord in that system, who controlled land and the peasants who worked it.
fact: In the informal sense, «feudal» means old-fashioned and unfair, with a few powerful people controlling many others.
fact: Phrases you will meet: «the feudal system», «feudal society», «feudal lord».
exercise: In history, what was the feudal system? | *The way society was organised in medieval Europe, with kings, lords and peasants | A kind of school for knights | A modern way to pay taxes | A type of castle made of wood
exercise: «The survivors could ask for higher pay, and the old feudal system began to crack.» What does feudal mean here? | Happy and free | *Belonging to the old system where lords controlled land and peasants | Covered in snow | Very quick and modern
exercise: Which word in «the old feudal system began to crack» shows the system belonged to the past? | higher | crack | survivors | *old
test: A feudal lord was given land by the king in return for what? | Free holidays | Gold and jewels only | *Loyalty and soldiers | Taking lessons
test: Tom says his school rules are feudal, meaning old-fashioned and unfair. What does feudal mean here? | Giving out light | Very large | Belonging to a castle | *Old-fashioned and unfair, with a few powerful people in control
exam: The phrase «feudal society» most likely describes what? | A sea voyage to a new land | A school full of pupils | *A society organised around lords, land and loyalty in medieval Europe | A modern city with trains and cars
